protected TableDefinition adjustTableFormat(final TableDefinition table) {
        final List<TextStyle.Builder> styleBuilders = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < table.columnTextStyles().size(); i++) {
            final TextStyle style = table.columnTextStyles().get(i);
            final TextStyle.Builder builder = TextStyle.builder().setTextStyle(style);
            styleBuilders.add(builder);
            final String header = table.headers().get(i);

            if (style.getMaxWidth() < header.length() || style.getMaxWidth() == TextStyle.UNSET_MAX_WIDTH) {
                builder.setMaxWidth(header.length());
            }
            if (style.getMinWidth() < header.length()) {
                builder.setMinWidth(header.length());
            }
            for (final List<String> row : table.rows()) {
                final String cell = row.get(i);
                if (cell.length() > builder.getMaxWidth()) {
                    builder.setMaxWidth(cell.length());
                }
            }
        }
        // calculate the total width.
        int calcWidth = 0;
        int adjustedMaxWidth = textStyleBuilder.getMaxWidth();
        for (final TextStyle.Builder builder : styleBuilders) {
            adjustedMaxWidth -= builder.getLeftPad();
            if (builder.isScalable()) {
                calcWidth += builder.getMaxWidth();
            } else {
                adjustedMaxWidth -= builder.getMaxWidth();
            }
        }
        // rescale if necessary
        if (calcWidth > adjustedMaxWidth) {
            final double fraction = adjustedMaxWidth * 1.0 / calcWidth;
            for (int i = 0; i < styleBuilders.size(); i++) {
                final TextStyle.Builder builder = styleBuilders.get(i);
                if (builder.isScalable()) {
                    // resize and remove the padding from the maxWidth calculation.
                    styleBuilders.set(i, resize(builder, fraction));
                }
            }
        }
        // regenerate the styles
        final List<TextStyle> styles = new ArrayList<>();
        // adjust by removing the padding as it was not accounted for above.
        styleBuilders.forEach(builder -> styles.add(builder.get()));
        return TableDefinition.from(table.caption(), styles, table.headers(), table.rows());
    }

explanation:
The `adjustTableFormat` function will compute the necessary adjustments to the widths of the columns in a `TableDefinition` based on the headers and the contents of the rows. The function will ensure that the total width of the table does not exceed a specified maximum width, resizing scalable columns proportionally if necessary. The method will return a new `TableDefinition` with updated styles reflecting these adjustments.

Here's how the implementation will work:
1. Validate the input `table` to ensure it is not null and contains valid headers and rows.
2. Calculate the maximum width required for each column based on the length of the headers and the contents of the rows.
3. Determine the total width of the table and compare it with the maximum allowed width.
4. If the total width exceeds the maximum, adjust the widths of the columns proportionally.
5. Create a new `TableDefinition` with the adjusted styles and return it.

```java
protected TableDefinition adjustTableFormat(final TableDefinition table) {
    if (table == null || table.headers() == null || table.rows() == null || table.headers().isEmpty()) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid TableDefinition: must not be null and must contain headers and rows.");
    }

    List<String> headers = table.headers();
    List<TextStyle> styles = table.columnTextStyles();
    List<Integer> columnWidths = new ArrayList<>();
    int totalWidth = 0;

    // Calculate the maximum width for each column based on headers and row contents
    for (int i = 0; i < headers.size(); i++) {
        int maxWidth = headers.get(i).length();
        for (List<String> row : table.rows()) {
            if (row.size() > i) {
                maxWidth = Math.max(maxWidth, row.get(i).length());
            }
        }
        columnWidths.add(maxWidth);
        totalWidth += maxWidth + styles.get(i).getLeftPad(); // Adding left padding
    }

    // Define the maximum allowed width
    int maxAllowedWidth = getMaxWidth(); // Assuming this method returns the maximum width for the table

    // If total width exceeds max allowed width, adjust column widths proportionally
    if (totalWidth > maxAllowedWidth) {
        double scaleFactor = (double) maxAllowedWidth / totalWidth;
        for (int i = 0; i < columnWidths.size(); i++) {
            int newWidth = (int) Math.round(columnWidths.get(i) * scaleFactor);
            styles.get(i).setMaxWidth(newWidth);
        }
    } else {
        // Set the styles to the calculated widths
        for (int i = 0; i < columnWidths.size(); i++) {
            styles.get(i).setMaxWidth(columnWidths.get(i));
        }
    }

    return TableDefinition.from(table.caption(), styles, headers, table.rows());
}
