public static int indexOfWrap(final CharSequence text, final int width, final int startPos) {
        if (width < 1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Width must be greater than 0");
        }
        // handle case of width > text.
        // the line ends before the max wrap pos or a new line char found
        int limit = Math.min(startPos + width, text.length());
        for (int idx = startPos; idx < limit; idx++) {
            if (BREAK_CHAR_SET.contains(text.charAt(idx))) {
                return idx;
            }
        }
        if (startPos + width >= text.length()) {
            return text.length();
        }

        limit = Math.min(startPos + width, text.length() - 1);
        int pos;
        // look for the last whitespace character before limit
        for (pos = limit; pos >= startPos; --pos) {
            if (Util.isWhitespace(text.charAt(pos))) {
                break;
            }
        }
        // if we found it return it, otherwise just chop at limit
        return pos > startPos ? pos : limit - 1;
    }

explanation:
The `indexOfWrap` function is designed to find an appropriate index in a `CharSequence` where a line break can occur, based on a specified width and starting position. The function first checks for any break characters (defined in `BREAK_CHAR_SET`) within the specified width from the `startPos`. If no break characters are found, it searches for the last whitespace character within that range. If neither is found, it defaults to returning the limit minus one. The function must also handle edge cases such as when the width exceeds the length of the text or when no valid break points are found.

```java
public static int indexOfWrap(final CharSequence text, final int width, final int startPos) {
    if (width < 1) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("width must be greater than 0");
    }
    if (text == null) {
        throw new NullPointerException("text must not be null");
    }
    int limit = Math.min(startPos + width, text.length());
    int breakPos = -1;

    for (int i = startPos; i < limit; i++) {
        char c = text.charAt(i);
        if (BREAK_CHAR_SET.contains(c)) {
            return i; // Found a break character
        }
        if (Character.isWhitespace(c)) {
            breakPos = i; // Remember the last whitespace position
        }
    }

    return breakPos != -1 ? breakPos : limit - 1; // Return last whitespace or limit - 1
}
